### custom minifirewall commands
#
# You can add any custom command in files like this;
# either this one, or others in the same directory.
# They are executed as shell scripts.
# They are automatically included in alphanumerical order.
# 
# Within included files, you can use those helper functions :
# * is_ipv6_enabled: returns true if IPv6 is enabled, or false
# * is_docker_enabled: returns true if Docker mode is enabled, or false
# * is_proxy_enabled: returns true if Proxy mode is enabled, or false
#
# Allow TCP input from 192.0.2.1 to port 1234 :
# /sbin/iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --sport 1024:65535 --dport 1234 -s 192.0.2.1 -j ACCEPT
#
# Allow TCP output to 192.0.2.1 to port 1234 :
# /sbin/iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 1024:65535 --sport 1234 -s 192.0.2.1 -m state --state ESTABLISHED -j ACCEPT
#
# Block 192.0.2.1 completely :
# /sbin/iptables -I INPUT -s 192.0.2.1 -j DROP
